  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "The number of digits in the number \\(N=2^{12}\\times5^8\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each pair of factors \\(2\\) and \\(5\\) makes \\(10\\). There are eight such pairs, leaving four factors of \\(2\\), so\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nN&=2^4\\cdot2^8\\cdot5^8\\\\\n &=16\\cdot(2\\cdot5)^8\\\\\n &=16\\cdot10^8.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nMultiplying \\(16\\) by \\(10^8\\) appends eight zeros. Thus \\(N\\) has \\(2+8=\\boxed{10}\\) digits, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
